# Dashboard drive receipt — presentation pass

Context: the frontend/dashboard pass. Build: `build/web/` rebuilt by `bash web/build.sh`
from the current headers (Emscripten 6.0.12, `-O2 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic`; `web/main.cpp`
also compiles clean under `-Werror`). Sources: [web/](../../web) — `shell.html`,
`showcase.css`, `core.js`, `scenes.js`, `render.js`, `instrument.js`, `showcase.js`,
`main.cpp`. The engine headers, the scene factories and the default PGS path are untouched.

Page: `http://127.0.0.1:8777/index.html`, served with
`python -m http.server 8777 --bind 127.0.0.1` from `build/web`.

## Method

Every driven number below came from the engine's own pause + single-step path:

    Module._toggle_pause()  -> pause
    Module._step_once(); Module._tick_js()   -> exactly one World::step(1/60)

The suite asserts `#stepCount` equals the number of driver iterations (it checks 5 after
five calls and 30 after thirty), so a throttled `requestAnimationFrame` cannot inflate the
figures. `#stepCount` reads `g_steps`, incremented once per `World::step` in `tick()`.

The preview tab also reported `visibilityState = "visible"` while its webview was not being
composited, so `requestAnimationFrame` was starved and the frame buffer went stale between
driver calls. That is why one control change needs a rendered frame (or an explicit
`_tick_js()`) before the counts in the panel reflect it; the suite waits on the frame buffer
rather than on the engine flag for exactly this reason. Nothing here is derived from the
stale path.

## Live observations (thread preview, real clicks)

Driven through the actual UI surface, not through `page.evaluate` shortcuts:

| action | observed |
|---|---|
| scene nav click `Stress 5000` | title, category, body count and `#sceneTitle` switch; `#iterations` reseeds to 10, `#ngs` presses on, `#sleeping` presses on — i.e. the panel mirrors the stress factory rather than keeping the cradle's 40 / NGS-off |
| scene-change wipe | `getComputedStyle(#stageWipe).animationName === "wipe"` at the moment of the switch |
| `Sleeping` toggle click | `Module._sleeping_enabled()` 0 and `#sleeping[aria-pressed=false]`; the settled field goes 0 → 5,000 awake |
| `Stage profile` click | `#phaseSource` `PROFILE OFF` → `PROFILE ON`, panel undims, all seven rows populate |
| canvas click with `+ Box` armed | bodies 5,001 → 5,002 through the pointer handler; `#toolHint` read `Click to place a box…` and `#spawnBox[aria-pressed=true]` |
| `preview_logs` (console + network) | empty after driving; the previous `/favicon.ico` 404 is gone because the icon is now an inline SVG data URI |

Observed dashboard read-out while the stress field was awake with sleeping disabled:
`BODIES 5,001`, `AWAKE 5,000`, `ASLEEP 0`, `STATIC 1`, `CONTACT POINTS 10,000`,
`PHYSICS STEP · EMA 13.12 ms`, `WITHIN BUDGET` at 39.4% of a two-budget bar,
`Σ 13.00 ms / 13.12 ms`, and stage shares
`bookkeeping 44.2% (5.75 ms)`, `broadphase 28.2% (3.67 ms)`, `solve 20.5% (2.66 ms)`,
`narrowphase 6.4% (0.83 ms)`, `integrate 0.7% (0.09 ms)`, `islands 0 µs`, `ccd 0.00 ms`.
`islands` is exactly zero because island sleeping was off — an independent cross-check that
the bucket labels mean what they say.

## Measurements (dashboard suite and calibration probes)

| configuration | bodies | awake | contacts | step EMA | stage detail |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| stress, sleeping off | 5001 | 5000 | 10000 | 13.1–17.9 ms | bookkeeping 5.75 ms (44%), broadphase 3.67 ms, solve 2.66 ms |
| stress, iterations 10 → 120 | 5001 | 5000 | 10000 | 43.1–47.3 ms | solve 2.84 → 31.00 ms; over budget, `#statePill` gains `strain` |
| stress, NGS off (iterations 120) | 5001 | 5000 | 10000 | 35.7 ms | bookkeeping 6.57 → 0.43 ms |
| stress, settled and sleeping | 5001 | 0 | 1000 | 6.4–8.0 ms | gauge falls back to 20.7% |
| wrecking pyramid, defaults | 213 | 211 | 970 | 7.10 ms | Σ 7.07 ms: solve 2.96, bookkeeping 3.50, broadphase 0.31 |
| momentum row, gravity slider set to +9.81 | 5 | 5 | 0 | — | max height 1.27 m after 30 steps |

Stage reconciliation held on both loaded cases: Σ 13.00 ms vs 13.12 ms and Σ 14.19 ms vs
14.35 ms, i.e. ~99% accounted. The residual is unmeasured time between clock reads.

### Host load moved every figure by more than 2x

The suite was then re-run with the machine loaded. Same build, same scene, same driver:

| case | quiet run | loaded run |
|---|---:|---:|
| stress, sleeping off, 5000 awake | 13.1–17.9 ms | 26–28 ms |
| stress, iterations 120 | 43.1–47.3 ms | 112.5 ms |
| settle stage: solve, iterations 10 | 2.84 ms | 7.74 ms |
| settle stage: solve, iterations 120 | 31.00 ms | 83.15 ms |
| settled, sleeping on | 6.9 ms | 13.7 ms |

That is why the suite's assertions are relational — sleeping cheaper than awake, the gauge
equal to the step it was given, the stage sum reconciling with the step, the solve stage
growing with the iteration count — and not millisecond thresholds. An earlier draft asserted
`settled gauge < 40%` and failed at 41.1% on the loaded run; it was replaced, not loosened.

## What this does and does not show

- It is the **WebAssembly** build. These numbers are not interchangeable with
  `build/active.csv`, which is native, and neither set is a rendered frame rate — the step
  cost excludes the canvas paint by construction.
- The tuning controls are proven to write through to the solver (iterations, NGS, sleeping,
  gravity each verified by reading the engine back), and two of them are proven to change the
  measured stage split. That is evidence the panel is wired to the engine, not evidence that
  any particular setting is a good one.
- NGS-off collapsing `bookkeeping` (5.8–7.6 ms → 0.4–0.5 ms) corroborates the native finding
  that position projection dominates an active contact graph. It does not decompose
  `bookkeeping`, which also contains row building and the impulse-cache save.
- The stage split is **opt-in and off by default**, so the default step pays no measurement
  overhead. With it on, the clock reads are themselves work.
- Small scenes resolve nothing: a six-body step is shorter than the browser's coarsened clock,
  so the stage rows read `BELOW CLOCK QUANTUM`. That is the timer, not the engine.
- The visual review used the thread preview at a narrow viewport plus Playwright captures at
  1440/1024/390 (`dash-desktop.png`, `dash-tablet.png`, `dash-mobile.png` and their
  `-panel` variants). The preview webview stopped compositing partway through the session, so
  the later captures were taken by Playwright headless instead.

